================================================================================
PART A  the loader measurement, with the command that produces it
================================================================================
The parent log states that 102 entries carry 22 red fixtures and 27 fcov manifests and zero carry both, which is
what makes the defect latent rather than live, but it does not say how that was measured. Stating a figure without
its command is the exact fault of the CM205-Low-1 row answered in the same touch, so here is the command and its
output. It calls the loader and the shipped predicate rather than re-implementing either, so a rename of the
testlist field cannot leave this count quietly wrong.

The command is written out in full below rather than cited by path, because Runtime's work directory is gitignored
and a command citing a file that no commit carries is not re-runnable by a reviewer. Paste it at the clone root
after sourcing ci/env.sh; the output beneath it is that command's own.

  python3 - dv/auto_dv/flow/gen_testlist.yaml <<'PY'
  import sys
  from pathlib import Path
  sys.path.insert(0, "dv/auto_dv/flow")
  import gen_flow_util as U
  tl = U.load_testlist(Path(sys.argv[1]).resolve())
  t = tl["tests"]
  both = [x["name"] for x in t if U.red_grading_deferred(x)]
  print("entries                       : %d" % len(t))
  print("red_fixture entries           : %d" % sum(1 for x in t if x.get("red_fixture")))
  print("fcov_expectation_file entries : %d" % sum(1 for x in t if x.get("fcov_expectation_file")))
  print("red_grading_deferred (both)   : %d  %s" % (len(both), both))
  PY

  output:
    entries                       : 102
    red_fixture entries           : 22
    fcov_expectation_file entries : 27
    red_grading_deferred (both)   : 0  []

  measured against the committed testlist at e988ee6; the three counts climb as
  entries land, and the fourth is the one the claim rests on: it must stay 0 until the standing guard is added,
  and become exactly 1 when it is.

